<div class="section">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <h2 class="reveal" style="text-align:center;">Your Teachers</h2>

    <div class="practitioners">
      <div class="practitioner-card reveal">
        <img src="/img/Jsq.jpg" alt="Jenny" class="practitioner-photo">
        <div class="practitioner-name">Jenny</div>
        <div class="practitioner-role">Yoga & Sound Healing</div>
        <p class="practitioner-bio">Jenny is a Registered Yoga Teacher (RYT) with Yoga Alliance, bringing over a decade of dedicated experience in yoga practice and teaching, with particular expertise in Therapeutic Yoga and Restorative Yoga. She has been teaching Yoga at UNI Yoga Academy at senior tutor level in Vietnam, leading and contributing to numerous 200-hour and 500-hour Yoga Teacher Training programmes, with Restorative Yoga as a core component of her curriculum. In recent years she has expanded her practice into Sound Healing, completing extensive training in therapeutic sound, breathwork and meditation. Known for her calm presence and authentic approach, these skills inform every class she teaches and every joint session she delivers with other teachers.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="practitioner-card reveal">
        <img src="/img/Ssq.jpg" alt="Seb" class="practitioner-photo">
        <div class="practitioner-name">Seb</div>
        <div class="practitioner-role">Qigong & Raja Yoga</div>
        <p class="practitioner-bio">Seb brings over two decades of training in Asian healing arts. He has practised Yoga since 1997, studying with masters in Japan and India, and is a certified Yoga teacher through IYF Asia, qualified in South Korea. Since 2010 he has trained intensively in authentic Qigong, studying and practising with masters across Mainland China, Hong Kong, Japan, Indonesia, Thailand and Scotland. He is also a certified Therapeutic Thai bodywork therapist and instructor, accredited by TTMA Japan since 2018, with deep additional study in TCM Reflexology. Seb has taught at senior tutor level at the Traditional Thai Massage Association Japan and at the Shivaga Traditional Medical School in Japan, where he delivered Therapeutic Thai Bodywork, Reflexology and Qigong. His deep understanding of Qi cultivation, the principles of Traditional Chinese Medicine as they relate to energy work, and hands-on therapeutic bodywork informs every class and session he delivers. Beyond the realm of practice and teaching, Seb is an initiate and direct disciple in the Inchegiri Navnath Sampradaya lineage (Nisargadatta Maharaj, Ramakant Maharaj).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="practitioner-card reveal">
        <img src="/img/Asq.jpg" alt="Amy" class="practitioner-photo">
        <div class="practitioner-name">Amy</div>
        <div class="practitioner-role">Yoga & Sound Healing</div>
        <p class="practitioner-bio">Amy is a certified Yoga teacher with 500-hour training and five years of dedicated teaching experience, specialising in Restorative Yoga, Yin Yoga and Sound Healing. She has worked extensively with international clients, bringing a calm and intuitive approach to sessions designed for relaxation, recovery and deep inner balance. Her Yin Yoga classes use long-held postures to release tension held deep in the connective tissue, while her Sound Healing work uses vibrational resonance to support the body's natural capacity for rest and repair. Amy creates a warm, unhurried space where students can slow down and reconnect with themselves at their own pace.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
